# The search of the skins (D281) on the water box of
# pme-settle.test with the groups: `MDIR_SKIN_SEARCH=always` measures the
# reference of D261 (12 / 9.6 Å) and the candidates of the cost model,
# keeps one, and caches it; a second run and a continuation take it from
# the cache, and neither a run of another time step nor one whose loop over
# pairs prunes (MDIR_FUSED_PRUNE=always) does. The run with the
# reaches chosen misses no pair within the cutoff (MDIR_CHECK_PRUNING,
# D268), and its energies at the start are those of the defaults to the
# digits of the log in double precision: the skins change the speed, not
# the pairs. The deterministic mode does not search, so that its bits
# repeat; across skins it agrees to the rounding, not to the bit, since the
# order of a row of the matrix follows its cells.
#
# The record of the search (D[skin-budget-record]): the entry and the
# manifest hold the budget and the candidates; the second run, with the
# compile cache that the first one filled, reuses the choice and says so,
# with the first one's candidates, rather than searching again. The key
# names the build (MDIR_COMPILE_CACHE_SALT_OVERRIDE, another build, misses), and an entry
# of format 1, one that is cut short, one without its budget, or one whose
# choice is not among its candidates is refused (`mdir check` notes it).
# A run that affords fewer than 3 candidates (MDIR_SKIN_SEARCH=budget, 100
# steps) caches nothing, and its manifest gives the budget and why.
#
# REQUIRES: cuda, hdf5
#
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: cp %S/Inputs/opc/opc.prmtop %S/Inputs/opc/opc.inpcrd %t
# RUN: sed -n '/^#--- run.toml/,/^#--- end/p' %S/pme-settle.test | sed '1d;$d' \
# RUN:     | sed -e 's|^pairlist_distance = 10.0|pairlist_distance = "AUTO"\npruned_distance = "AUTO"|' \
# RUN:           -e 's|^steps *= 100|steps = 100|' \
# RUN:           -e 's|energy_interval = 50|energy_interval = 50\ncheckpoint = "run.h5"\ncheckpoint_interval = 100\nmanifest = "run.json"|' \
# RUN:           -e 's|^type = "PERIODIC"|type = "PERIODIC"\n[execution]\ntarget = "gpu"\nprecision = "double"\nneighbor_structure = "GROUPS"|' > %t/auto.toml
# RUN: sed -e 's|^steps = 100|steps = 200|' %t/auto.toml > %t/longer.toml
# RUN: sed -e 's|^time_step *= 0.001|time_step = 0.0005|' %t/auto.toml > %t/half.toml
# RUN: cd %t && env MDIR_COMPILE_CACHE_DIR=%t/cc MDIR_SKIN_CACHE=on MDIR_SKIN_CACHE_DIR=%t/cache MDIR_SKIN_SEARCH=always MDIR_CHECK_PRUNING=1 mdir run auto.toml > first.log 2> first.err
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=FIRST < %t/first.log
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CHECKED < %t/first.err
# RUN: %python -c "import json; e = json.loads(open('%t/run.json').readline())['effective']; s = e['skin_search']; print(e['pairlist_distance_source'], e['pruned_distance_source'], s['source'], len(s['candidates']) >= 3, bool(s['cache']), s['searched'], s['budget'], s['budget_basis']['policy'])" | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MANIFEST
# RUN: cp %t/run.json %t/first.json
# RUN: %python -c "import glob, json; e = json.load(open(glob.glob('%t/cache/*.json')[0])); print(e['format'], e['key'].splitlines()[:2], e['search']['budget'], len(e['search']['candidates']))" | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ENTRY
# An entry written before D396, whose reason spells the
# angstrom in Unicode, is read as any other: the reader takes the key and
# the two reaches alone.
# RUN: %python -c "import glob, json; f = glob.glob('%t/cache/*.json')[0]; e = json.load(open(f, encoding='utf-8')); e['search']['reason'] = '1.0% faster than 12 / 9.6 \u00c5, beyond the noise of 0.6%'; json.dump(e, open(f, 'w', encoding='utf-8'), ensure_ascii=False)"
# RUN: cd %t && env MDIR_COMPILE_CACHE_DIR=%t/cc MDIR_SKIN_CACHE=on MDIR_SKIN_CACHE_DIR=%t/cache MDIR_SKIN_SEARCH=always mdir run auto.toml > second.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CACHED < %t/second.log
# The second run reused the first one's choice and search, to the bit of
# each candidate's time: a search again would have timed them anew. Its
# recorded reason is the one written into the entry above.
# RUN: %python -c "import json; a, b = (json.loads(open(f, encoding='utf-8').readline())['effective'] for f in ('%t/first.json', '%t/run.json')); s, t = a['skin_search'], b['skin_search']; print(t['source'], t['searched'], t['seconds'], t['budget'] == s['budget'], t['candidates'] == s['candidates'], t['budget_basis'] == s['budget_basis'], t['recorded_reason'] == '1.0% faster than 12 / 9.6 \u00c5, beyond the noise of 0.6%', (a['pairlist_distance_angstrom'], a['pruned_distance_angstrom']) == (b['pairlist_distance_angstrom'], b['pruned_distance_angstrom']))" | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=REUSED
# RUN: cd %t && env MDIR_SKIN_CACHE=on MDIR_SKIN_CACHE_DIR=%t/cache MDIR_SKIN_SEARCH=always mdir run --continue longer.toml > continued.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CONTINUED < %t/continued.log
# RUN: cd %t && env MDIR_SKIN_CACHE=on MDIR_SKIN_CACHE_DIR=%t/cache MDIR_SKIN_SEARCH=never mdir run half.toml > half.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MISSED < %t/half.log
# RUN: ls %t/cache | wc -l | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ONE
# The guards of the entry, through `mdir check`, which measures nothing:
# the entry is taken; another build's salt misses it; an entry of format
# 1, without a format, cut short, without its budget, or whose choice is
# not among its candidates is refused. The entry is restored after each.
# RUN: cp %t/cache/*.json %t/entry.saved
# RUN: cd %t && env MDIR_SKIN_CACHE=on MDIR_SKIN_CACHE_DIR=%t/cache mdir check auto.toml 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=TAKEN
# RUN: cd %t && env MDIR_COMPILE_CACHE_SALT_OVERRIDE=another-build MDIR_SKIN_CACHE=on MDIR_SKIN_CACHE_DIR=%t/cache mdir check auto.toml 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SALT --implicit-check-not=refused
# RUN: %python -c "import glob, json; f = glob.glob('%t/cache/*.json')[0]; e = json.load(open(f)); e['format'] = 1; json.dump(e, open(f, 'w'))"
# RUN: cd %t && env MDIR_SKIN_CACHE=on MDIR_SKIN_CACHE_DIR=%t/cache mdir check auto.toml 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=REFUSED,FORMAT1
# RUN: %python -c "import glob, shutil; shutil.copy('%t/entry.saved', glob.glob('%t/cache/*.json')[0])"
# RUN: %python -c "import glob, json; f = glob.glob('%t/cache/*.json')[0]; e = json.load(open(f)); del e['format'], e['search']['budget']; json.dump(e, open(f, 'w'))"
# RUN: cd %t && env MDIR_SKIN_CACHE=on MDIR_SKIN_CACHE_DIR=%t/cache mdir check auto.toml 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=REFUSED,NOFORMAT
# RUN: %python -c "import glob, shutil; shutil.copy('%t/entry.saved', glob.glob('%t/cache/*.json')[0])"
# RUN: %python -c "import glob; f = glob.glob('%t/cache/*.json')[0]; t = open(f).read(); open(f, 'w').write(t[:len(t) // 2])"
# RUN: cd %t && env MDIR_SKIN_CACHE=on MDIR_SKIN_CACHE_DIR=%t/cache mdir check auto.toml 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=REFUSED,CUT
# RUN: %python -c "import glob, shutil; shutil.copy('%t/entry.saved', glob.glob('%t/cache/*.json')[0])"
# RUN: %python -c "import glob, json; f = glob.glob('%t/cache/*.json')[0]; e = json.load(open(f)); del e['search']['budget']; json.dump(e, open(f, 'w'))"
# RUN: cd %t && env MDIR_SKIN_CACHE=on MDIR_SKIN_CACHE_DIR=%t/cache mdir check auto.toml 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=REFUSED,NOBUDGET
# RUN: %python -c "import glob, shutil; shutil.copy('%t/entry.saved', glob.glob('%t/cache/*.json')[0])"
# RUN: %python -c "import glob, json; f = glob.glob('%t/cache/*.json')[0]; e = json.load(open(f)); e['pairlist_distance_angstrom'] += 0.25; json.dump(e, open(f, 'w'))"
# RUN: cd %t && env MDIR_SKIN_CACHE=on MDIR_SKIN_CACHE_DIR=%t/cache mdir check auto.toml 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=REFUSED,NOTCHOSEN
# RUN: %python -c "import glob, shutil; shutil.copy('%t/entry.saved', glob.glob('%t/cache/*.json')[0])"
# RUN: cd %t && env MDIR_SKIN_CACHE=on MDIR_SKIN_CACHE_DIR=%t/cache mdir check auto.toml 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=TAKEN
# A run that affords fewer than 3 candidates: the reference alone, nothing
# cached, and the budget and why in the manifest.
# RUN: sed -e 's|run.json|budget.json|' -e 's|run.h5|budget.h5|' %t/auto.toml > %t/budget.toml
# RUN: mkdir -p %t/cache-budget
# RUN: cd %t && env MDIR_SKIN_CACHE=on MDIR_SKIN_CACHE_DIR=%t/cache-budget MDIR_SKIN_SEARCH=budget mdir run budget.toml > budget.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BUDGET < %t/budget.log
# RUN: ls %t/cache-budget | wc -l | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=NONE
# RUN: %python -c "import json; s = json.loads(open('%t/budget.json').readline())['effective']['skin_search']; print(s['source'], s['searched'], s['budget'], s['budget_basis']['policy'], len(s['candidates']), s['cache']); print(s['not_cached']); print(s['reason'])" | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BUDGET-MANIFEST
# Whether the loop over pairs prunes (D284) is part of the key.
# RUN: cd %t && env MDIR_FUSED_PRUNE=always MDIR_SKIN_CACHE=on MDIR_SKIN_CACHE_DIR=%t/cache MDIR_SKIN_SEARCH=never mdir run auto.toml > fused.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=FUSEDKEY < %t/fused.log
# The defaults, and the chosen reaches, at the start.
# RUN: cd %t && env MDIR_SKIN_SEARCH=never mdir run auto.toml > never.log 2>&1
# RUN: cat %t/never.log %t/first.log | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SAME
# The deterministic mode: the matrix, no search, the same bits twice, and
# another reach to the rounding.
# RUN: sed -e 's|^neighbor_structure = "GROUPS"|deterministic = true|' -e 's|run.json|deterministic.json|' %t/auto.toml > %t/deterministic.toml
# RUN: sed -e 's|run.h5|again.h5|' %t/deterministic.toml > %t/again.toml
# RUN: sed -e 's|run.h5|reach.h5|' -e 's|^pairlist_distance = "AUTO"|pairlist_distance = 11.5|' %t/deterministic.toml > %t/reach.toml
# RUN: cd %t && rm -f run.h5 && env MDIR_SKIN_SEARCH=always mdir run deterministic.toml > deterministic.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=DETERMINISTIC < %t/deterministic.log
# RUN: cd %t && env MDIR_SKIN_SEARCH=always mdir run again.toml > again.log 2>&1
# RUN: mdir checkpoint %t/run.h5 %t/again.h5 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BITS
# RUN: cd %t && mdir run reach.toml > reach.log 2>&1
# RUN: not mdir checkpoint %t/run.h5 %t/reach.h5 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ROUNDING

# FIRST: MDIR: skins: candidate 12 / 9.6 Ang: {{[0-9.]+}} us a step
# FIRST: MDIR: skins: candidate {{[0-9.]+}} / {{[0-9.]+}} Ang: {{[0-9.]+}} us a step
# FIRST: MDIR: skins: candidate {{[0-9.]+}} / {{[0-9.]+}} Ang: {{[0-9.]+}} us a step
# FIRST: MDIR: skins: the reach {{[0-9.]+}} Ang, pruned to {{[0-9.]+}} Ang (measured: {{.*}}; searched now: a budget of 7, {{[3-7]}} candidates in {{[0-9.]+}} s; stored in '{{.*}}cache/{{[0-9a-f]+}}.json')
# FIRST: MDIR: the inner lists were pruned
# CHECKED: mdrt: the inner lists were checked at {{[0-9]+}} steps: {{[1-9][0-9]+}} pairs within the cutoff, none missed
# MANIFEST: measured measured measured True True True 7 always
# ENTRY: 2 ['mdir skins 2', 'mdir-skin-salt 1'] 7 {{[3-7]}}
# CACHED: MDIR: skins: the reach {{[0-9.]+}} Ang, pruned to {{[0-9.]+}} Ang (cached: the choice of an earlier run of the same key; reused, not searched: the search of a budget of 7 recorded {{[3-7]}} candidates in {{[0-9.]+}} s; from '{{.*}}cache/{{[0-9a-f]+}}.json')
# REUSED: cached False 0 True True True True True
# CONTINUED: MDIR: continues the run after step 100
# CONTINUED: MDIR: skins: {{.*}} (cached:
# MISSED: MDIR: skins: the reach 10.5 Ang (default: MDIR_SKIN_SEARCH=never)
# FUSEDKEY: MDIR: skins: {{.*}}(default: MDIR_SKIN_SEARCH=never)
# ONE: {{^}}1{{$}}
# TAKEN: skins: cached (the choice of an earlier run of the same key)
# SALT: skins: default (a short run:
# REFUSED-DAG: skins: default (a short run:
# FORMAT1-DAG: mdir: note: the entry '{{.*}}cache/{{[0-9a-f]+}}.json' of the cache of the skins is refused: its format is 1, not 2;
# NOFORMAT-DAG: mdir: note: the entry '{{.*}}' of the cache of the skins is refused: it names no format, as one of format 1 did;
# CUT-DAG: mdir: note: the entry '{{.*}}' of the cache of the skins is refused: it is not JSON
# NOBUDGET-DAG: mdir: note: the entry '{{.*}}' of the cache of the skins is refused: its search lacks a budget of at least 3;
# NOTCHOSEN-DAG: mdir: note: the entry '{{.*}}' of the cache of the skins is refused: the chosen reaches are not among its candidates;
# BUDGET: MDIR: skins: candidate 12 / 9.6 Ang: {{[0-9.]+}} us a step
# BUDGET-NOT: MDIR: skins: candidate
# BUDGET: MDIR: skins: the reach 12 Ang, pruned to 9.6 Ang (default: a candidate costs {{[0-9]+}} s, and the run of about {{[0-9]+}} s affords 0 within 2% of it, fewer than 3; not searched: the reference alone measured, in {{[0-9.]+}} s, a budget of 0; not cached: the budget of 0 is below 3, so that a longer run of the same key may still search)
# NONE: {{^}}0{{$}}
# BUDGET-MANIFEST: default False 0 budget 1 None
# BUDGET-MANIFEST-NEXT: the budget of 0 is below 3, so that a longer run of the same key may still search
# BUDGET-MANIFEST-NEXT: a candidate costs {{[0-9]+}} s, and the run of about {{[0-9]+}} s affords 0 within 2% of it, fewer than 3
# SAME: MDIR:   total {{ *}}[[TOTAL:-?[0-9]+\.[0-9]+]]
# SAME: MDIR: skins: {{.*}} (measured:
# SAME: MDIR:   total {{ *}}[[TOTAL]]
# DETERMINISTIC: MDIR: skins: the reach 10.5 Ang (default: the deterministic mode)
# BITS: the states are identical
# ROUNDING: values of the positions differ, by up to {{[0-9.]+}}e-{{(09|1[0-9])}}
